[
    {
        "content": "<p>Hi everyone,</p>\n<p>I have been having trouble working with model-theoretic types in Lean. If I understand it correctly, in the current version of Mathlib, a complete n-type is implemented as a set of <code>L[[Fin n]].Sentences</code><br>\nrather than a set of objects of type  <code>L.Formula (Fin n)</code></p>\n<p>My question is: Given an object <code>φ</code> of type <code>L.Formula (Fin n)</code>, how can I express a membership relation like <code>φ ∈ p</code> if <code>p</code> has type <code>T.CompleteType (Fin n)</code> for some L-Theory T? </p>\n<p>Simply typing <code>φ ∈ p</code> does obviously not work, just as <code>(φ : L[[Fin n]].Sentence) ∈ p</code> doesn't because Lean cannot automatically cast between the types <code>L.Formula (Fin n)</code> and <code>L[[Fin n]].Sentence</code>.</p>",
        "id": 591105642,
        "sender_full_name": "Ruth Plümer",
        "timestamp": 1777288290
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Did <span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"779253\">Matteo Cipollina</span>'s answer in the other thread help?</p>\n<p><a class=\"message-link\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/113489-new-members/topic/Quantifying.20over.20all.20free.20variables.20in.20a.20Formula/near/591111873\">#new members &gt; Quantifying over all free variables in a Formula @ 💬</a></p>",
        "id": 591194227,
        "sender_full_name": "Matt Diamond",
        "timestamp": 1777311244
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>naively it seems like you could convert an <code>L.Formula (Fin n)</code> to an <code>L.Sentence</code> by quantifying over all the free variables (as Matteo described) and then convert the <code>L.Sentence</code> to a <code>L[[Fin n]].Sentence</code> using a language map, but I'm not sure if that's what you're trying to do</p>",
        "id": 591198439,
        "sender_full_name": "Matt Diamond",
        "timestamp": 1777312467
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>No, unfortunately that is not what I am trying to do... I want to consider the free variables in the <code>L.Formula (Fin n)</code> as constants, therefore making the <code>L.Formula (Fin n)</code> an <code>L[[Fin n]].Formula</code> without free variables, i.e. an <code>L[[Fin n]].Sentence</code></p>",
        "id": 591198951,
        "sender_full_name": "Ruth Plümer",
        "timestamp": 1777312610
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The other thread was about a different problem that wasn't related to model theoretic types</p>",
        "id": 591199148,
        "sender_full_name": "Ruth Plümer",
        "timestamp": 1777312666
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>here's what I came up with</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FirstOrder</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Language</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Theory</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Formula</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">CompleteType</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">))</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(((</span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">lhomWithConstants</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">onFormula</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">φ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">subst</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">con</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">term</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 591201629,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1777313326
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>oh this is even better</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FirstOrder</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Language</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Theory</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Formula</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">CompleteType</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">))</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FirstOrder</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Language</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Formula</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">equivSentence</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 591202030,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1777313444
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>nice!</p>",
        "id": 591202176,
        "sender_full_name": "Matt Diamond",
        "timestamp": 1777313490
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks, that is exactly what I was looking for!</p>",
